) should supply the anodes of these indicator LEDs so they can be lit.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"/LED_3.3V_POWER_SW : D14.2(A,passive) D23.2(A,passive) D4.2(A,passive)\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"Net-(D23-K) : D23.1(K,passive) R3.1(passive)\"}], \"impact\": \"Ethernet link/activity and Pi activity indicators stay dark because their anodes have no supply, so the status indication is lost.\", \"confidence\": 0.3}], \"summary\": \"The netlist has two indicator-LED faults. The second channel of the ESTOP_OUT dual LED D30 has its anode and series resistor R60 both on ESTOP_OUT, so it cannot light. The anodes of D4, D14 and D23 sit on a net with no driver. Neither issue is mentioned in the specification, and both are plausible wiring errors that affect only status indication.\"}",
